# NSMBW Rust port: scripts/1-1.press with four players (P6's 4-player check).
# Wii Remotes 1-4, held sideways (D-pad down is screen right, 2 jumps, 1 runs).
# nsmbw-port --unpaced --press-file scripts/1-1-4p.press --frames 11000
# Needs an existing save in file 1, as 1-1.press does.

# Strap screen, title, file select.
600:a 1550:2 2600:2
# Remotes 2-4 switch on (a remote is on from its first press).
p2:2000: p3:2000: p4:2000:
# Select Players: Number of Players 1 -> 3 (left) -> 4 (down; the first down
# lands while the cursor still moves), then OK.
2800:left 2840:down 2880:down 2950:2
# 4 Players: Luigi, Yellow Toad and Blue Toad press 2 (OK); then Start Game.
p2:3050:2 p3:3090:2 p4:3130:2 3400:2
# Walk out to the World 1 map and enter 1-1 (as in 1-1.press; with four
# players the map comes at ~3600, without the opening cutscene).
5150:down:900 6100:2

# 1-1: all four players hold right and run, and hop on 1-1.press's frames,
# then every 40 frames to the flagpole. They die and come back in bubbles
# along the way; Luigi reaches the flagpole at ~10250, the course is
# cleared at ~10400, and by 11000 all four are back on the World 1 map.
# The presses end before the map, so nothing walks on into 1-2.
6300:down+1:4100
p2:6300:down+1:4100
p3:6300:down+1:4100
p4:6300:down+1:4100
6300:2:20 6340:2:20 6380:2:20 6420:2:20 6460:2:20 6500:2:20 6540:2:20 6580:2:20 6620:2:20 6660:2:20 6700:2:20 6740:2:20 6780:2:20 6820:2:20 6844:2:20 6884:2:20
